<article class="env-lemma" id="064E">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/064E">Lemma <span data-tag="064E">13.19.11</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Let $\beta : P^\bullet \to L^\bullet $ and $\alpha : E^\bullet \to L^\bullet $ be maps of complexes. Let $n \in \mathbf{Z}$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$P^\bullet $ is a bounded complex of projectives and $P^ i = 0$ for $i < n$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$H^ i(\alpha )$ is an isomorphism for $i > n$ and surjective for $i = n$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then there exists a map of complexes $\gamma : P^\bullet \to E^\bullet $ such that $\alpha \circ \gamma $ and $\beta $ are homotopic. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Consider the cone $C^\bullet = C(\alpha )^\bullet $ with map $i : L^\bullet \to C^\bullet $. Note that $i \circ \beta $ is zero by Lemma <a href="/tag/064D" data-tag="064D">13.19.10</a>. Hence we can lift $\beta $ to $E^\bullet $ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0149" data-tag="0149">13.4.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>